  "id": "subjectivity",
  "term": "subjectivity",
  "definition": "Subjectivity is the first-person aspect of experience in which a world is organized from the subject’s own point of view. In the source, it is described as a structure where a third-person world appears within a first-person world, producing egocentric knowledge that also includes the subject.",
